## Rules

- Apply the code changes and add/update tests as described in the plan.
- Do not clutter the code with comments. Add a comment only when it is
  genuinely needed to explain non-obvious logic, and write such comments
  in Russian. Do not restate what the code already says, and do not leave
  narration or step-by-step commentary.
- Run the relevant test suite; if it fails, fix it until it goes green.
- Try to find and run the project's linter/formatter if one is configured.
- The phase will create the commit itself after you finish. Do NOT run
  any git command that mutates the repo (`add`, `commit`, `push`, `checkout`, ...)
  — these will be blocked.
- Read-only git commands ARE allowed and encouraged for orienting yourself
  (`status`, `diff`, `log`, `show`, ...).
- Do not edit anything outside the worktree, and do not create a merge
  request.

## Output

When you are done, emit a final reply containing the XML-tagged block below,
exactly:

```
<commit_message>
<one short, imperative subject line summarizing this change>
</commit_message>
```

Rules for the commit message:
- a single line, max 72 characters
- imperative mood ("Add X", "Fix Y" — not "Added"/"Fixes")
- describe the change at the level of intent, not low-level edits
- no trailing period, no surrounding quotes
- do NOT write a literal `</commit_message>` inside the block contents —
  the parser stops at the first match.
